<%# decor/app/views/admin/component_suggestions/index.html.erb %>
<%# version 1.4 %>
<%# v1.4: UI rename — column header "Order Number" -> "DEC Part Number". %>
<%#   Historical comments below (Session 67/68) describing the column under its %>
<%#   old label are left as-is for accuracy; only the live header text changed. %>
<%# Session 68 (cont'd): v1.2's fix (dropping the page-local max-w-6xl) only %>
<%#   removed this page's OWN extra width cap — the shared admin layout's %>
<%#   <main class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-6 py-6"> was still capping the page at %>
<%#   1280px, which was still visibly too narrow on wider screens. Confirmed %>
<%#   scope with the user: this page only, no fixed maximum at all (not just a %>
<%#   wider fixed cap), without changing the shared layout. Switched the outer %>
<%#   div to a "full-bleed" pattern (relative left-1/2 right-1/2 w-screen %>
<%#   -mx-[50vw]) that breaks out of the parent's max-w-7xl and spans the full %>
<%#   viewport width on any screen size. See the inline comment on the div %>
<%#   itself for the mechanism and a minor scrollbar-width caveat. %>
<%# Session 68: Two layout changes requested for this page specifically: %>
<%#   1. "Unused margins too wide" — the outer wrapping div carried its own %>
<%#      "max-w-6xl mx-auto" on top of the admin layout's "max-w-7xl mx-auto" %>
<%#      (decor/app/views/layouts/admin.html.erb <main>), so this page was %>
<%#      rendering narrower than the layout it sits inside. Removed the %>
<%#      page-local max-w-6xl/mx-auto so the page now fills the full width %>
<%#      already provided by the shared admin layout. Deliberately NOT %>
<%#      touching admin.html.erb itself — that would widen every admin page, %>
<%#      not just this one, which was not requested. %>
<%#   2. "Order Number column 25% wider" — added table-fixed + a <colgroup> so %>
<%#      column widths are explicit percentages instead of auto-sized by %>
<%#      content. See the inline comment above the <colgroup> for the exact %>
<%#      baseline assumption and the resulting widths. %>
<%# Session 67: Phase 4 item 4 rewrite. Root cause of the slow page load %>
<%# (Session 66 finding, confirmed by code review this session): v1.0 had NO %>
<%# pagination and NO filtering — it rendered every ComponentSuggestion row %>
<%# unconditionally (@component_suggestions.each over the full table), which %>
<%# at ~55,000 rows (Phase 4 data scope) made the page slow to load even %>
<%# though rendering, once loaded, was fine. %>
<%# %>
<%# Changes from v1.0: %>
<%#   - Wrapped the table in a grid grid-cols-4 layout: _filters partial takes %>
<%#     col-span-1 (leftmost column); table takes col-span-3 — same layout %>
<%#     contract as software_items/index.html.erb v1.1. %>
<%#   - @component_suggestions.each replaced with @page.records.each — %>
<%#     @page is what Pagination#paginate actually sets (confirmed by reading %>
<%#     decor/app/controllers/concerns/pagination.rb this session), NOT an %>
<%#     ivar named after the model. %>
<%#   - Row markup extracted into _component_suggestion.html.erb so %>
<%#     index.turbo_stream.erb can reuse it for "Load more" appends. %>
<%#   - Added a "Manual" column (Phase 4 item 1) — see the row partial for %>
<%#     the em-dash-for-nil convention. %>
<%#   - "Load more" render added at the bottom of the table column, %>
<%#     confirmed Session 67 to match the existing infinite-scroll pattern %>
<%#     rather than classic pagination. %>
<%# %>
<%# @page            — geared_pagination page object (set by paginate() in %>
<%#                     Admin::ComponentSuggestionsController#index v1.2) %>
<%# @page_title      — "Component Suggestions" %>
<%# @turbo_tbody_id  — "component_suggestions" %>
<%# @load_more_id    — "load_more_component_suggestions" %>
<%# @index_path      — admin_component_suggestions_path with current query/manual %>
<%#                     filter params preserved %>
<%# %>
<%# Session 63: Phase 1 of Component Suggestions feature. %>
<%# Includes New, Edit, and Delete actions. Pattern: mirrors %>
<%# admin/software_names/index.html.erb for the CRUD actions, and %>
<%# software_items/index.html.erb (Session 50) for the filter+pagination grid. %>

<div class="relative left-1/2 right-1/2 w-screen -mx-[50vw] px-6 mt-8">
  <%# v1.3 full-bleed technique: "relative left-1/2 right-1/2 w-screen -mx-[50vw]" %>
  <%# breaks this div out of the admin layout's centered "max-w-7xl mx-auto" %>
  <%# container (decor/app/views/layouts/admin.html.erb <main>) and gives it the %>
  <%# actual viewport width (100vw) instead of a percentage of its parent — so %>
  <%# it uses all current screen width with no fixed maximum, on any screen size, %>
  <%# without touching the shared layout or affecting any other admin page. %>
  <%# px-6 (matches the nav's own horizontal padding) replaces the page's %>
  <%# previous reliance on the layout's inherited px-6 for left/right breathing %>
  <%# room, since this div no longer sits inside that padded <main>. %>
  <%# CAVEAT: 100vw includes the browser's vertical scrollbar width, which can %>
  <%# cause a few px of horizontal overflow on some browsers/OSes. Not addressed %>
  <%# here since it's a minor, browser-dependent cosmetic edge case — flag if it %>
  <%# becomes visible in practice and I'll add a scrollbar-width compensation. %>
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-6">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-800"><%= @page_title %></h1>
    <%= link_to "New Component Suggestion",
                new_admin_component_suggestion_path,
                class: "inline-flex items-center px-4 py-2 bg-indigo-600 text-white text-sm font-medium rounded hover:bg-indigo-700" %>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-4 gap-4 items-start">
    <%# Filter sidebar — col-span-1 is set inside the partial's form class. %>
    <%= render "filters" %>

    <%# Table — takes the remaining 3 columns. %>
    <div class="col-span-3">
      <% if @page.records.any? %>
        <table class="w-full table-fixed text-sm text-left">
          <%# table-fixed + colgroup added (Session 68) so column widths are explicit %>
          <%# percentages rather than auto-sized by content — a prerequisite for making %>
          <%# "Order Number +25% wider" a well-defined, verifiable change rather than a %>
          <%# vague nudge that the browser's auto layout might not honour predictably. %>
          <%# %>
          <%# ASSUMPTION (no prior explicit widths existed to derive this from): %>
          <%# chosen baseline widths were Order Number 16% / Description 40% / %>
          <%# Category 16% / Manual 12% / Actions 16% (=100%). Applying the requested %>
          <%# +25% to Order Number: 16% * 1.25 = 20%. The 4-point difference is taken %>
          <%# from Description (40% -> 36%), the column with the most room to spare, %>
          <%# so the other three columns are left untouched. Resulting widths: %>
          <%#   Order Number 20% | Description 36% | Category 16% | Manual 12% | Actions 16% %>
          <colgroup>
            <col style="width: 20%">
            <col style="width: 36%">
            <col style="width: 16%">
            <col style="width: 12%">
            <col style="width: 16%">
          </colgroup>
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-200">
              <th class="pb-2 pr-6 text-stone-500 uppercase text-xs font-medium">DEC Part Number</th>
              <th class="pb-2 pr-6 text-stone-500 uppercase text-xs font-medium">Description</th>
              <th class="pb-2 pr-6 text-stone-500 uppercase text-xs font-medium">Category</th>
              <th class="pb-2 pr-6 text-stone-500 uppercase text-xs font-medium">Manual</th>
              <th class="pb-2 text-stone-500 uppercase text-xs font-medium">Actions</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <%# tbody id is set from @turbo_tbody_id so index.turbo_stream.erb can append to it. %>
          <tbody id="<%= @turbo_tbody_id %>" class="divide-y divide-stone-100">
            <% @page.records.each do |suggestion| %>
              <%= render "component_suggestion", suggestion: suggestion %>
            <% end %>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      <% else %>
        <p class="text-stone-500 mt-4">No component suggestions match these filters.</p>
      <% end %>

      <%# Load-more partial — renders a "Load more" button when more pages exist. %>
      <%# @index_path includes current filter params so pagination preserves filters. %>
      <%= render "shared/load_more", id: @load_more_id, page: @page, path: @index_path %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
